WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.649 --> 00:00:05.600
Hi, my name is Macy Phung.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.509
Today I will be telling you the 5 signs you
are ready to share your personal story with

00:00:11.509 --> 00:00:12.840
an audience.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.530
My life is a dance.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:20.410
I experienced mania which is happiness and
sunshine.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:28.130
And on the other end I experienced depression
which is sadness and my melodic song becomes

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.130
mellow.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:39.110
In between we have the intricate symbols from
the universe and everything is intertwined.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:49.080
You can see my illness quote unquote schizoaffective
disorder is not a curse but rather a blessing

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.160
in disguise.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:55.640
Without further ado I will be telling you
my personal story.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:01:02.490
My mother and father grew up during the Vietnam
War in China and Vietnam where they experienced

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:03.840
poverty and unrest.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:11.690
Then they immigrated to America for the American
Dream where my sister, brother and I had better

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.280
opportunities.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.900
In high school I was very shy.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:23.040
I was not confident however I very hard to
get good grades because I know how much my

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.720
parents sacrificed for us.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:35.460
By the time I was 18 years old I was diagnosed
with schizoaffective disorder which in my

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:39.780
case is a combination of schizophrenia and
manic depression.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:46.340
I experienced my first blow of mania and I
was elated and happy.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:52.500
I could share my opinions without caring about
other people’s perceptions of me.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:02.670
During this time I really bonded with my family
for the first time, especially my sister.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:03.670
She was there for me every step of the way.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:11.879
She took me out on outings and she treated
me as a good sister would.

00:02:11.879 --> 00:02:19.129
I wanted to capture my experience so I decided
to make my very first short film called A

00:02:19.129 --> 00:02:27.299
RIPPLE IN TIME which is about two sisters
and the uncertainty which lies with schizoaffective

00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:30.279
disorder and the future.

00:02:30.279 --> 00:02:37.040
Our film was praised and commended Film Festival
in San Francisco and I knew that I wanted

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.510
to hold on to this moment.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:47.700
At that point I knew that I wanted to be a
filmmaker, that is my dream.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:56.099
The Universe gave me symbols and it told me
that my mission in life is to end poverty

00:02:56.099 --> 00:02:59.299
with awareness though dance by 2030.

00:02:59.299 --> 00:03:07.959
I carried this mission with me everywhere
but for several years I was so lonely.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:12.829
I had no team members.

00:03:12.829 --> 00:03:17.049
I was just on my own and then I got into a
huge episode of depression.

00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:19.779
I could not get out of bed for weeks on end.

00:03:19.779 --> 00:03:23.590
I could not bring myself to do anything.

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:30.559
However I stayed true to myself and as they
say “When the people is ready, the master

00:03:30.559 --> 00:03:32.209
arrives.”

00:03:32.209 --> 00:03:41.170
I was opened and welcomed into communities
who accepted me as I am.

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.730
They are caring and they are kind.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:51.459
Of course it’s through me being courageous,
stepping out of my comfort zone and putting

00:03:51.459 --> 00:03:57.159
in a great deal of effort that my communities
continue to encourage me to grow and feed

00:03:57.159 --> 00:04:01.769
off of each other’s positive energy.

00:04:01.769 --> 00:04:08.299
Okay so now that I’ve told you my personal
story I would like to share with you 5 signs

00:04:08.299 --> 00:04:11.859
you are ready to share your personal story
with an audience.

00:04:11.859 --> 00:04:15.519
Number 1 - you have immersed in your story.

00:04:15.519 --> 00:04:17.790
You have lived it.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:20.500
When was the last time you really, truly felt
alive?

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.970
For me it was when I experienced mania.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:33.599
To be alive means you experience happiness
longing wants creativity and you meet a lot

00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:37.419
of people along the way who shape your life
path.

00:04:37.419 --> 00:04:43.930
Of course at this stage you also have to have
reflected on your experiences and feelings

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.570
as well as your emotions.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:57.289
Number 2 - You are able to tell your personal
story in front of a lot of different people

00:04:57.289 --> 00:05:00.900
at networking events and social gathering.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:07.110
As a filmmaker I naturally have to share my
personal story and pitch it.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:14.300
A lot of times what I do at these networking
events, I tell my story and at this time it

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:16.379
is a quite a bit of uncertainty.

00:05:16.379 --> 00:05:23.729
I am not sure if people are interested in
my story, if they resonate with me or if they

00:05:23.729 --> 00:05:25.310
are even interested in talking to me.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:31.539
And most of the time I felt that the answer
was no.

00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:38.759
However, further along my life journey I realized
that conversation is a two-way street.

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:46.280
You have to listen to the other person’s
story and you have to find an alignment.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:51.550
Number 3 - You are comfortable with your story.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:06:01.690
At this stage I didn’t care about what people
felt about my personal story at all.

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:12.199
At this point in my life I am able to just
say it truly and genuinely and when I radiate

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:17.450
this confidence I fell in love with the world
and it loved me right back.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:21.710
It is a wonderful, magical feeling.

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:31.250
Number 4 - At this stage you are able to tell
your personal story in front of a big audience

00:06:31.250 --> 00:06:36.930
full of people or online through viewers and
readers.

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:44.680
I’m able to be vulnerable and be true to
myself and put my whole self out there.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:52.550
A lot of people have expressed gratitude to
me for sharing my story.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:07:01.900
Number 5 - Last but not least you feel your
biggest dreams and ambitions within your reach.

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:08.380
As a filmmaker my dream is to make my drama
feature film DANCE FOR WORLD PEACE based on

00:07:08.380 --> 00:07:09.979
my personal story.

00:07:09.979 --> 00:07:17.210
I’m able to keep going on my dream every
single day despite constant challenges and

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:21.159
heartbreaking stings and rejection.

00:07:21.159 --> 00:07:28.110
You just keep going and going and going and
you have faith that one day your dreams will

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.750
come true.

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:38.010
At this time you also have to have a place
of peace and for me and for me that is Alameda

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:42.280
Beach where I have grown up.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:47.099
Your life story is always evolving all the
way up until your last breath.

00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:48.060
Thank you.

